{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01908",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.08,
      "end_seconds": 4.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "hi, is it okay to come in now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.89,
      "end_seconds": 10.16,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 11.76,
      "end_seconds": 23.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.91,
      "text": "It's swollen lips at times. I thought I'd wait, uh, but it hasn't gone. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.31,
      "end_seconds": 31.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.01,
      "end_seconds": 41.77,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "For about a week, I'd say. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.27,
      "end_seconds": 53.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Okay, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.07,
      "end_seconds": 73.52,
      "duration_seconds": 18.45,
      "text": "Pretty severe, if I'm being honest. I'd say all the time. Oh, and poor sleep from itching. As for poor sleep from itching, maybe a four out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.78,
      "end_seconds": 74.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "I follow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.36,
      "end_seconds": 82.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "I did have welts that move around at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.61,
      "end_seconds": 89.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Have you had swollen lips at times before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.76,
      "end_seconds": 97.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.37,
      "end_seconds": 104.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Have you noticed fever, joint pain, throat tightness or difficulty breathing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.49,
      "end_seconds": 109.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "None of those, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.63,
      "end_seconds": 118.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.28,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.59,
      "end_seconds": 124.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "My heart's been fine, as far as I know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.68,
      "end_seconds": 144.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.53,
      "end_seconds": 157.62,
      "duration_seconds": 11.09,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours. My partner and our baby. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.48,
      "end_seconds": 162.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.44,
      "end_seconds": 167.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "Yes, heart failure. I have diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.01,
      "end_seconds": 173.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.03,
      "end_seconds": 179.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Yes, grass pollen, it gives me sneezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.66,
      "end_seconds": 193.07,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.71,
      "end_seconds": 195.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "no surgery, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.66,
      "end_seconds": 199.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "right, tell me your medicines, please"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.78,
      "end_seconds": 209.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Right, I take glimepiride, 2 milligrams, before breakfast. Cetirizine, 10 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.13,
      "end_seconds": 214.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.8,
      "end_seconds": 217.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "no, it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 231.89,
      "end_seconds": 241.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature is 36.4 degrees, pressure 122 over 68. Saturation 97 percent, pulse 74."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.34,
      "end_seconds": 244.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.01,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.47,
      "end_seconds": 251.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "I'll need to examine you for this, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.3,
      "end_seconds": 255.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.5,
      "end_seconds": 259.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Raise your arm for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.36,
      "end_seconds": 278.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "there are pink raised wheals on the arms and trunk that blanch with pressure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.84,
      "end_seconds": 310.82,
      "duration_seconds": 29.98,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Having listened and examined, this looks most like chronic spontaneous urticaria. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. Another possibility is a food reaction. I want blood tests done, that's for chronic urticaria. Let's use fexofenadine, 180 milligrams, once a day, long term. That should help with urticaria. Keep a diary of foods and triggers and avoid hot showers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.49,
      "end_seconds": 319.9,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.28,
      "end_seconds": 329.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.81,
      "text": "I follow and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.07,
      "end_seconds": 336.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.07,
      "text": "Thank you, that's clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.98,
      "end_seconds": 343.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.5,
      "text": "Come back in six weeks. Anything else on your mind before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.17,
      "end_seconds": 348.61,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Uh, okay, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.63,
      "end_seconds": 351.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}